{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they shall place upon it a covering of tachash skin, and spread over it a garment entirely of tekhelet above</b> — Because of the preeminence of the Ark, the tachash-skin covering was not visible upon it. Rather, they would cover it with the parokhet (curtain), which is its screen, and cover them both with a covering of tachash skin because of the rain, and spread a garment entirely of tekhelet over everything above, so that the distinguished garment would be visible upon it — which is like the essence of the heavens for purity (Numbers Rabbah 4:13). But for the rest of the vessels — the Table, the Menorah, and the Altars — the tachash-skin covering was visible upon them from above.\n\nThere are those who say that the reason of the verse is: \"and they shall spread a garment entirely of tekhelet above\" — for the parokhet that serves as the screen, \"and they shall place upon it\" — upon the Ark and the parokhet — \"a covering of tachash skin.\"\n\nThe meaning of <b>and they shall put its staves</b> — on the shoulders of the priests. The correct interpretation is that they would fix them so as to protrude for carrying it by them, for the rings were wide and they could extend the staves in them as they wished, provided they not be removed from it."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The citation marker (במד״ר ד י׳ג) refers to Bamidbar Rabbah (Numbers Rabbah) 4:13."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:32.632293142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}